From 96077c44a82e283a096a2efa401837b88b8d9046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:15:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Batch: jacobians of meshes without nodes computed by a kernel

The jacobians of the element transformations of a mesh without nodes were
computed by the geometric factors of MFEM from a copy of the vertices in a
finite element space of order one. Building this space and projecting the
coordinates on it cost about 1.8 s on the host for 1.6 million tetrahedra,
once per integration rule, which was 60% of the time of a stationary heat
transfer computed by kernels on the GPU.

The jacobians and their determinants are now computed by a kernel from the
vertices of the elements and the gradients of the shape functions of the
finite element of the transformations of MFEM
(`mfem::Mesh::GetTransformationFEforElementType`), whose degrees of
freedom are the vertices of the elements in their order. The mesh is still
not modified. Meshes with nodes still use the geometric factors of the
mesh. `ElementsGeometry` exposes the jacobians and the determinants as
vectors, owned by the mesh or by the geometric data.

ElementsGeometryTest compares the jacobians, their determinants and the
weights to the element transformations of MFEM for segments, triangles,
quadrangles, tetrahedra, hexahedra, wedges and pyramids, regular and
distorted, with unknowns of order one and two, and for a curved mesh, on
the host, on the debug device and on the GPU.

Stationary heat transfer of the prototype (280 000 unknowns, 5 steps), on
the GPU: 3.01 s to 1.25 s.
